# Copy to `.env` beside the manifest. The real environment always wins over this file.
#
# Pick one preset. The manifest does not change between them — that portability is the whole
# claim of the model layer, and it is what the Phase 1 acceptance criteria check.

# ── OpenAI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
MODEL_ID=gpt-4o-mini
MODEL_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
MODEL_API_KEY=

# ── Anthropic, via its OpenAI-compatible endpoint ─────────────────────────────────────────
# MODEL_ID=claude-sonnet-4-20250514
# MODEL_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1
# MODEL_API_KEY=

# ── DeepSeek ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `deepseek-chat` for ordinary work; `deepseek-reasoner` to see reasoning stream separately
# (run with --show-reasoning). The reasoner ignores temperature, so drop it from the manifest
# rather than wondering why it has no effect.
# MODEL_ID=deepseek-chat
# MODEL_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
# MODEL_API_KEY=

# ── Local Ollama — no key needed, so delete `apiKeyEnv` from the manifest or set any value ─
# MODEL_ID=qwen3.5:9b
# MODEL_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# MODEL_API_KEY=ollama
